BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (The NTFS volume boot sector contains geometry and the starting logical cluster numbers of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (the Master File Table \($MFT\) and its mirror. The $MFT contains variable-sized file record) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (segments. Each file is represented by at least one record; even NTFS metadata files such) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (as $MFT, $Bitmap and $LogFile are represented as files. Records contain typed attributes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 608.0 Tm (which may be resident within the MFT record or nonresident elsewhere on the volume.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (A file record starts with a signature and a fixup array used to detect incomplete sector) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (writes. Attributes include $STANDARD_INFORMATION, $FILE_NAME, $DATA and other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (type-specific records. Nonresident attributes use mapping pairs or runlists to identify) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 527.0 Tm (extents. Multiple named $DATA streams may belong to one file. NTFS's internal structure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 510.0 Tm (must not be flattened to a single inode plus sequential sectors.) Tj ET
