BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (NTFS invests more metadata and CPU work than FAT to support security, indexing, sparse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (data, resident attributes and independent metadata streams. The attribute system permits) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (incremental evolution without changing every directory structure. Runlist compression and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (variable-sized resident records complicate a forensic implementation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 595.0 Tm (Features such as EFS encryption, compression, deduplication and reparse points can require) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (Windows-specific services or metadata interpretation. A parser able to enumerate basic MFT) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (entries is not automatically a safe complete writer, and a native Linux module must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (qualify each supported attribute family separately.) Tj ET
